WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:06.400
A fleet of eight computers heats an apartment whose own heating is switched off.

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:18.000
Every five minutes Orrery reads two thermometers in the room and the weather at the airport, works out how many watts the room wants moved, and takes one step:

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:24.000
a lane of work paused or resumed, or a machine powered off and later woken.

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:33.400
Since 16:44 on the seventeenth of November it holds that room at eighty degrees Fahrenheit, by itself.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:35.000
The ceiling is eighty-one.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:43.400
In the first fifteen hours the room went to about eighty-one point six, once, and a person had to end it.

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:45.000
How is it used?

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:46.600
What is it calculating?

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:48.600
Did it hold the room?

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:51.400
What does it need from a person?

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:55.200
Keeping the Room.

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:59.200
How to use, read and look after Orrery's thermal regulation.

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:02.600
Part one.

00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:04.200
How to use it.

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:07.600
In Orrery:

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:08.800
Queue, then Heat.

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:11.200
The Heat page has six panels.

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:13.600
The first two are for this.

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:15.200
Hearth is the controls.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:16.800
Diagram is the picture:

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:21.200
where the heat comes from, where it goes, and the thermometers.

00:01:23.800 --> 00:01:31.000
To set the temperature, press minus or plus zero point five, or type a number and press Return.

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:32.600
Too warm right now?

00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:35.000
Lower the target by a degree.

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:37.000
A door opened is faster.

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:40.400
Three modes.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:40.800
Off:

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:43.600
nothing is read and nothing is done.

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:44.000
Advise:

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:49.200
every five minutes it says what it would do, and changes no machine.

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:49.600
Act:

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:50.800
it does it.

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:55.200
The button is framed in red and must be pressed twice.

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:57.200
To take over, press advise.

00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:59.200
Lanes it paused stay paused.

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:06.600
The power row has a cell for each machine, and one button.

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:08.600
On sends the wake packet.

00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:09.800
Off, pressed twice:

00:02:09.800 --> 00:02:14.600
the machine finishes its job, leaves the queue, and is powered off.

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:18.200
The machine that carries the thermometers has no Off.

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:22.600
The controller powers off only a machine known to come back.

00:02:22.600 --> 00:02:23.800
Three are proved.

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:30.400
The Hearth panel, at 08:19 on the eighteenth, in act.

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:30.800
One:

00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:32.800
the target, in both scales.

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:33.200
Two:

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:34.000
changing it.

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:34.400
Three:

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:35.200
the mode.

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:35.600
Four:

00:02:35.600 --> 00:02:36.800
the power switch.

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:41.200
It has no button; it is set from the command line.

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:41.600
Five:

00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:42.400
the hold:

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:47.200
the law in force, its budget in watts, and its last words.

00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:50.200
Six:

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:53.000
the power row, a cell a machine.

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:53.400
Seven:

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:54.600
the plan's age.

00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:57.400
Over fifteen minutes old, something has stopped.

00:02:57.400 --> 00:02:57.800
Eight:

00:02:57.800 --> 00:02:59.800
the room and its probes.

00:02:59.800 --> 00:03:00.200
Nine:

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:01.000
the balance.

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:05.800
Green is the watts drawn now; the mark is the watts wanted.

00:03:05.800 --> 00:03:06.200
Ten:

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:08.200
the ladder, the older law.

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:11.800
It does not act while the law is hold.

00:03:11.800 --> 00:03:15.000
The red paragraph says what act will do.

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:17.000
Read it before pressing act.

00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:22.000
The Diagram panel, two minutes later.

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:22.400
One:

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:24.400
the weather, the outer frame.

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:24.800
Two:

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:26.800
the walls, the hatched band.

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:29.200
The heat that leaves crosses it.

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:29.600
Three:

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:31.600
zone one, the fleet's room.

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:32.000
Four:

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:34.000
the machines, a tile each.

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:34.400
Five:

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:35.200
the collector.

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:37.600
A pipe's thickness is its watts.

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:40.600
Six:

00:03:40.600 --> 00:03:43.000
heat in, the fleet's total watts.

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:43.400
Seven:

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:45.400
the same, over six hours.

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:45.800
Eight:

00:03:45.800 --> 00:03:49.000
the air and the thermal mass, a tank.

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:55.000
It says soaking up when the room is warming, giving back when it is cooling.

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:55.400
Nine:

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:57.400
the room over three hours.

00:03:57.400 --> 00:03:57.800
Ten:

00:03:57.800 --> 00:04:01.000
other heat, everything that is not the fleet.

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:03.000
It is implied, not read.

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:06.000
Eleven:

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:09.600
zone two, the rest of the apartment, in dashes.

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:11.600
There is no thermometer there.

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:12.000
Twelve:

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:15.600
through the walls, the watts leaving to the weather.

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:16.400
Under it:

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:20.400
U A is a figure in use, not a measurement.

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:20.800
Thirteen:

00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:21.600
the thermometers.

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:22.000
Fourteen:

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:24.000
the balance, in one line.

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:28.000
The numbers change at each pass, about every five minutes.

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:31.400
Part two.

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:32.200
The science.

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:38.400
The room is treated as one lump of heat.

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:45.600
C times the room's slope equals the fleet's watts, plus every other watt, less what the walls lose.

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:48.400
The room and the weather are read.

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:54.000
So are the fleet's watts, with a model where a machine has no counter.

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:55.200
C is measured:

00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:57.600
four point two megajoules a degree.

00:04:57.600 --> 00:05:03.200
U A, the watts lost for each degree over the weather, is not measured.

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:06.800
One hundred and twenty is the figure in use.

00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:12.000
P nought, every watt that is not the fleet's, is not measured either.

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:14.400
It is what is left over.

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:18.200
Three things follow.

00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:19.800
Where the room settles:

00:05:19.800 --> 00:05:23.400
the weather, plus all the watts over U A.

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:24.200
How fast:

00:05:24.200 --> 00:05:25.800
C over U A.

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:30.600
Nine point seven hours, if U A is one hundred and twenty.

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:33.400
And the three flows on the Diagram.

00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:34.600
Through the walls:

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:37.800
U A times the gap to the weather.

00:05:37.800 --> 00:05:38.200
Soak:

00:05:38.200 --> 00:05:39.800
C times the slope.

00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:40.600
Other heat:

00:05:40.600 --> 00:05:43.000
walls plus soak, less the fleet.

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:46.200
It is as wrong as U A is.

00:05:48.800 --> 00:05:51.200
The controller does not use gains.

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:59.200
It asks how many watts must be added or taken away for the room to stop where it is wanted.

00:05:59.200 --> 00:06:05.600
The first term is what the walls will lose once the room is at the target.

00:06:05.600 --> 00:06:10.400
The second is what the room is storing as it moves now.

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:13.200
It is held within six hundred watts.

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:14.400
Then one step.

00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:20.800
Graphics machines are kept, and the machine that spends most energy on a job goes first.

00:06:20.800 --> 00:06:25.600
Forty minutes between changes, because the room answers about an hour late.

00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:30.600
A budget, on a quiet morning.

00:06:30.600 --> 00:06:38.200
The room at twenty-six point zero, the target twenty-six point seven, falling seven hundredths of a degree an hour.

00:06:38.200 --> 00:06:39.800
The U A term:

00:06:39.800 --> 00:06:41.000
minus eighty-four watts.

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:42.200
The C term:

00:06:42.200 --> 00:06:43.000
minus eighty-two.

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:43.800
The budget:

00:06:43.800 --> 00:06:46.200
plus one hundred and sixty-six watts.

00:06:46.200 --> 00:06:49.800
Every machine was already on, so nothing was done.

00:06:52.400 --> 00:06:54.400
A budget at its limit.

00:06:54.400 --> 00:07:00.000
The room at twenty-seven point one, rising zero point six nine degrees an hour.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:03.200
The U A term is only forty-eight watts.

00:07:03.200 --> 00:07:06.400
The C term is eight hundred and five.

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:10.400
Minus eight hundred and fifty-three, held at minus six hundred.

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:13.600
Not far over its target, but rising fast.

00:07:13.600 --> 00:07:18.800
A law that looked only at the error would have done almost nothing.

00:07:21.400 --> 00:07:24.600
The three flows on the Diagram, at 08:21.

00:07:24.600 --> 00:07:25.800
Through the walls:

00:07:25.800 --> 00:07:29.000
one hundred and twenty times fifteen point eight.

00:07:29.000 --> 00:07:31.000
Eighteen hundred and ninety-six watts.

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:31.400
Soak:

00:07:31.400 --> 00:07:32.600
seven hundred watts.

00:07:32.600 --> 00:07:33.400
Other heat:

00:07:33.400 --> 00:07:35.400
thirteen hundred and eighty-seven watts.

00:07:35.400 --> 00:07:41.000
It is implied, and it rests on a U A that is not measured.

00:07:43.600 --> 00:07:46.000
A night with every machine on.

00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:55.600
From two to seven the room stood at twenty-six point zero, the weather averaged five point seven, the fleet twelve hundred and eighty watts.

00:07:55.600 --> 00:08:00.400
So all the watts over U A are twenty point three degrees.

00:08:00.400 --> 00:08:04.800
If the other heat were nothing, U A would be sixty-three.

00:08:04.800 --> 00:08:06.400
That is a floor.

00:08:06.400 --> 00:08:13.200
If U A is one hundred and twenty, the other heat is eleven hundred and fifty-six watts.

00:08:13.200 --> 00:08:16.800
One steady night gives one equation in two unknowns.

00:08:19.400 --> 00:08:21.400
How cold can it be?

00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:24.600
The fleet's most is about thirteen hundred watts.

00:08:24.600 --> 00:08:31.800
The coldest weather at which eighty can be held is about six degrees Celsius, whatever the other heat.

00:08:31.800 --> 00:08:38.600
That night it went to three, and the room stood under its target with every machine working.

00:08:41.200 --> 00:08:42.000
Part three.

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:43.600
The first fifteen hours.

00:08:46.200 --> 00:08:48.200
Orrery took over at 16:44.

00:08:48.200 --> 00:08:50.600
Until 18:20 it held on target.

00:08:50.600 --> 00:08:54.600
Then the room rose zero point six degrees an hour.

00:08:54.600 --> 00:08:58.600
The law shed one hundred and forty-three watts, then seventy-three.

00:08:58.600 --> 00:09:00.600
A person shed the rest.

00:09:00.600 --> 00:09:03.400
The peak was about eighty-one point six.

00:09:03.400 --> 00:09:06.600
It fell back under the ceiling by 19:36.

00:09:06.600 --> 00:09:12.200
Overnight heat was added a step at a time, and the weather fell faster.

00:09:12.200 --> 00:09:18.200
From two to seven every machine was on, and the room stood under its target.

00:09:18.200 --> 00:09:19.800
Then the morning warmed.

00:09:19.800 --> 00:09:24.600
Seventy-eight point one to eighty-one point three by the controller's own reading.

00:09:27.200 --> 00:09:30.400
Eight faults were found by watching it run.

00:09:30.400 --> 00:09:36.400
One probe jumps a degree by itself, and a machine was switched off for it.

00:09:36.400 --> 00:09:41.600
A switch-off did not count as a change until the machine was down.

00:09:41.600 --> 00:09:44.000
Only named spares could be woken.

00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:48.400
Asked for six hundred watts, it shed one hundred and forty-three.

00:09:48.400 --> 00:09:52.000
At the ceiling, a spiking probe was not believed.

00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:54.800
The machine with the thermometers was paused.

00:09:54.800 --> 00:09:57.600
A large budget reached past small steps.

00:09:57.600 --> 00:10:00.400
Those seven were corrected the same day.

00:10:00.400 --> 00:10:02.000
The eighth is open:

00:10:02.000 --> 00:10:05.600
it should act on where the room is heading.

00:10:08.200 --> 00:10:09.000
Part four.

00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:11.000
How the heat is drawn.

00:10:13.600 --> 00:10:18.800
The Diagram is a process diagram, of the kind a control room uses.

00:10:18.800 --> 00:10:19.200
Nesting:

00:10:19.200 --> 00:10:22.800
the weather encloses the walls, the walls the apartment.

00:10:22.800 --> 00:10:24.800
Heat can only go outward.

00:10:24.800 --> 00:10:26.400
One colour, one meaning:

00:10:26.400 --> 00:10:31.600
yellow the fleet, orange the room, blue the weather, violet the other heat.

00:10:31.600 --> 00:10:32.800
Width is watts:

00:10:32.800 --> 00:10:34.800
a pixel for each seventy.

00:10:34.800 --> 00:10:36.000
Movement is direction.

00:10:36.000 --> 00:10:40.400
And a tank for what is stored, the term people forget.

00:10:43.000 --> 00:10:47.000
Hatching for the walls, dashes for what is not measured.

00:10:47.000 --> 00:10:47.800
Instrument bubbles:

00:10:47.800 --> 00:10:51.000
a ring is a thing that is read.

00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:56.600
The two numbers that rest on a guess say so, in the warning colour.

00:10:56.600 --> 00:10:59.400
Thermometers drawn as thermometers, on one scale.

00:10:59.400 --> 00:11:03.000
Trends beside the numbers, and clocks on every machine:

00:11:03.000 --> 00:11:06.200
three time scales are why the controller waits.

00:11:08.800 --> 00:11:13.200
The report before this one uses the same rules on paper:

00:11:13.200 --> 00:11:18.400
one time axis, one scale a chart, every line named at its end.

00:11:21.000 --> 00:11:21.800
Part five.

00:11:21.800 --> 00:11:22.200
Upkeep.

00:11:24.800 --> 00:11:27.200
Daily, look at the hold line:

00:11:27.200 --> 00:11:31.600
its plan under fifteen minutes old, its last words making sense.

00:11:31.600 --> 00:11:35.200
Weekly, save the weather and read the house's fit.

00:11:35.200 --> 00:11:38.000
A week missed is a week lost.

00:11:38.000 --> 00:11:41.600
After a power cut there is nothing to set.

00:11:41.600 --> 00:11:44.800
When a machine is added, prove it wakes.

00:11:47.400 --> 00:11:49.000
When something is wrong.

00:11:49.000 --> 00:11:51.400
The plan is twenty minutes old:

00:11:51.400 --> 00:11:53.000
is the keeper running?

00:11:53.000 --> 00:11:55.000
No room probe is fresh:

00:11:55.000 --> 00:11:56.600
restart radbeeper on saskatchewan.

00:11:56.600 --> 00:11:58.200
Over eighty-one and rising:

00:11:58.200 --> 00:12:02.600
lower the target, open a door, press Off on a Supermicro.

00:12:02.600 --> 00:12:04.600
Too cold and nothing left:

00:12:04.600 --> 00:12:06.200
every machine is on.

00:12:06.200 --> 00:12:07.400
Nothing to do.

00:12:07.400 --> 00:12:09.800
Jobs sent back every few minutes:

00:12:09.800 --> 00:12:11.000
close the app.

00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:13.000
The cause is not found.

00:12:15.600 --> 00:12:18.400
What is done, and what is not.

00:12:18.400 --> 00:12:24.800
The hold runs on the live fleet, in act, and held the room with one excursion.

00:12:24.800 --> 00:12:27.200
Seven of eight faults are corrected.

00:12:27.200 --> 00:12:29.600
Three machines are proved to wake.

00:12:29.600 --> 00:12:30.400
Not done.

00:12:30.400 --> 00:12:35.200
U A is not measured, and so neither is the other heat.

00:12:35.200 --> 00:12:37.200
Zone two has no thermometer.

00:12:37.200 --> 00:12:39.200
The eighth fault is open.

00:12:39.200 --> 00:12:42.400
The hold has no proof of its own:

00:12:42.400 --> 00:12:44.000
two days of running.

00:12:44.000 --> 00:12:48.400
And On and Off have not been pressed in the app.

00:12:51.000 --> 00:12:54.200
The fleet holds the room at eighty degrees.

00:12:54.200 --> 00:13:01.000
The house's loss per degree is still not measured, and everything that rests on it says so.
